{
  "version": "2.17",
  "children": [
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "oOZbE",
      "x": 880,
      "y": 0,
      "name": "Brief · Auth",
      "width": 360,
      "fill": "$bg-muted",
      "cornerRadius": "$radius-md",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": "$space-4",
      "padding": "$space-5",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "uPP4L",
          "name": "BT",
          "fill": "$fg-default",
          "content": "Auth — brief",
          "fontFamily": "$font-display",
          "fontSize": 18,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "BKJIf",
          "name": "BB",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Login + recovery for the single-user self-hosted instance. NO signup — the sole account is created at first-boot /setup (onboarding flow).\n\nEntry: root → /login. Recovery: /forgot-password → email → /reset-password/:token.\n\nScreens: Login (+ notice/error) · 2FA (TOTP) · Forgot password · Email sent · Reset password.\n\nRules: single account; TOTP 2FA (settled: password + TOTP, email OTP fallback, no SMS). Design-led, code is reference (D8).\n\nDesktop (1280): ONE artboard — Login, built as the SAME split-panel as onboarding's Setup (900 card = 420 brand + 480 form). They are the two doors into one instance and they now look alike; a plain centered card did not. The other four screens keep the centered-card treatment and inherit the form width — drawing them ×2 is the option D4 rejects.\n\nThe brand panel carries the mark and one line: '100% libre y open source'. Deliberately nothing else. Setup's panel has a title, a subtitle and a checklist because a wizard has something to promise; a login does not, and the product has no tagline that survived the pivot — the ones in the public footer and the meta tags ('Open Source Market Intelligence Platform', 'Private by Design') are pre-pivot copy for the audience ADR-0010 dropped. The claim used here is real: setup/new.html.erb:30 renders it, and onboarding.pen already carries its es-MX form. If the panel should say more, that is a copy decision for Adrian, not a blank to fill.\n\n🔴 D23 — the 2FA screen has no code and no decision behind it. This brief calls TOTP 'settled', but: no rotp or equivalent gem, no otp_secret/otp_required column on users, no route, no line of code anywhere in app/ or lib/ — and no entry in DECISIONS.md, no ADR, no CODE_CHANGES section, no GitHub issue. The only record of it existing is design/README.md listing the screen. Implementing it as drawn would repeat the notification-channel pattern: a UI offering something the instance cannot do. Worse for this product than for most — the instance has exactly one account and no support desk, so a lost authenticator locks Adrian out of his own server permanently unless recovery codes ship with it. Not a design call: logged as D23 for Adrian, and the screen stays drawn (design leads) but must not be built before the 4-filter card exists.\n\nCopy: es-MX. kit-version-source 0.1.0 (tokens only; this flow uses ButtonPrimary and Field, both unchanged since 0.1.0).",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
